      "id": "attribution",
      "type": "layout.comment",
      "name": "Original background-reference fixtures - MIT",
      "description": "Original MIT conveyor images, references, generator and projects by OpenCVDataflowGUI contributors; no external or customer data. A saved clean reference is replayed before the first current part is classified. Camera/calibration/grid/encoding bindings and SHA256 prevent accidental mismatches. Frozen MOG2 retains its native model. Frozen KNN rebuilds its query model because this wheel can update at learningRate=0. Guarded updates sanitize known foreground with trusted background pixels. Replay checks five independent current captures, including a persistent part and an empty last frame. Float MOG2 keeps original [0,255] fractional values. Camera mismatch intentionally errors before native work. Prepare reference writes only an explicitly requested generated JSON; never captures a scene with known foreground. This is reference replay, not opaque native-state serialization or physical camera qualification.",
